╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ beam_local_schedule_search                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ Replace sampled single-path greedy construction with a deterministic beam search followed │
│                          │ by insertion-based local optimization.                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. The prior method evaluates only a random subset of next transactions and commits       │
│                          │ immediately to one choice. A poor early commitment can create long read/write-conflict    │
│                          │ chains that cannot be repaired later.                                                     │
│                          │ 2. The new beam search keeps several promising partial transaction orders. Every retained │
│                          │ prefix is extended by every remaining transaction and scored through                      │
│                          │ `workload.get_opt_seq_cost`, which directly measures the conflict-aware scheduling        │
│                          │ objective rather than proxy properties such as transaction length.                        │
│                          │ 3. Retaining up to `num_seqs` prefixes allows the search to preserve alternatives when    │
│                          │ several early choices appear similar but lead to different downstream dependency delays.  │
│                          │ 4. Each completed beam candidate is refined with best-improvement insertion local search. │
│                          │ Moving one transaction across several others can remove conflict-critical ordering delays │
│                          │ that adjacent swaps or fixed greedy construction miss.                                    │
│                          │ 5. Costs are cached by sequence tuple, avoiding repeated simulator calls for identical    │
│                          │ prefixes or candidate schedules.                                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This remains valid because every generated candidate is a permutation of every            │
│                          │ transaction exactly once, while substantially broadening the search over transaction      │
│                          │ orders that determine makespan.                                                           │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0268                                                                                   │
