│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ regret_beam_descent                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ This version replaces the sampled greedy strategy with an evaluator-driven multi-start    │
│                          │ construction and local-descent optimizer.                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key steps:                                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Multiple deterministic/diverse starts:** Instead of committing to one random         │
│                          │ starting transaction, it constructs schedules from several starting transactions.         │
│                          │ 2. **Full marginal-cost selection:** At every construction step, every remaining          │
│                          │ transaction is evaluated as the next candidate. This directly uses `get_opt_seq_cost`, so │
│                          │ choices are based on actual conflict-induced makespan rather than transaction length or   │
│                          │ write counts.                                                                             │
│                          │ 3. **Best-seed selection:** The strongest constructed schedule is retained.               │
│                          │ 4. **Relocation descent:** The selected schedule is improved by repeatedly removing one   │
│                          │ transaction and testing every possible reinsertion position. This can repair poor early   │
│                          │ greedy choices and move transactions away from high-conflict regions.                     │
│                          │ 5. **Swap escape moves:** When relocation no longer improves the schedule, pairwise swaps │
│                          │ are tested to escape orderings that are locally optimal under insertion alone.            │
│                          │ 6. **Memoized cost evaluation:** Prefix and full-schedule makespan evaluations are        │
│                          │ cached, avoiding repeated simulator calls during construction and local search.           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The approach is fundamentally different from random candidate sampling: it treats the     │
│                          │ simulator as an exact objective oracle and performs a conflict-aware permutation search   │
│                          │ with both constructive diversification and schedule-level improvement.                    │
