│ patch_description        │ Replace random sampled greedy construction with deterministic beam search followed by     │
│                          │ makespan-based insertion local search.                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Cache every `get_opt_seq_cost` result, since both beam expansion and local improvement │
│                          │ repeatedly evaluate related schedules.                                                    │
│                          │ 2. Maintain several promising partial transaction orders rather than committing to one    │
│                          │ random first transaction. Every possible next transaction is evaluated using the          │
│                          │ simulator’s actual incremental schedule cost.                                             │
│                          │ 3. Keep a bounded, diverse beam of the lowest-cost partial schedules. This prevents an    │
│                          │ early locally attractive choice from permanently excluding better transaction conflict    │
│                          │ orderings.                                                                                │
│                          │ 4. Once complete schedules are obtained, improve each candidate using best-improvement    │
│                          │ relocation: remove one transaction and try it in every other position, accepting the move │
│                          │ that lowers the actual final makespan.                                                    │
│                          │ 5. `num_seqs` controls search breadth, while caps keep the approach practical for larger  │
│                          │ workloads. The result is selected exclusively by true makespan rather than transaction    │
│                          │ length or write-count proxies.                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This directly targets read/write conflict delay because every ordering decision and every │
│                          │ local move is scored by `workload.get_opt_seq_cost`.                                      │
