                         Patch Metadata - Gen 6/200 - Novelty: 1/3 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/3                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ elite_vnd_search                                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ Instead of applying expensive local search only to the single best greedy construction,   │
│                          │ retain a small elite set of the best independently constructed schedules and run          │
│                          │ variable-neighborhood descent on each.                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Step-by-step:                                                                             │
│                          │ 1. Greedy construction is sensitive to its starting transaction and may produce several   │
│                          │ schedules with similar initial makespan but very different local-search potential.        │
│                          │ 2. The currently selected best greedy schedule can be trapped in a local minimum that is  │
│                          │ worse than another elite schedule after relocation and swap optimization.                 │
│                          │ 3. Keep up to four lowest-cost constructed schedules as elite candidates.                 │
│                          │ 4. Apply the existing exact relocation and swap neighborhoods to every elite candidate.   │
│                          │ 5. Select the globally best improved result using the authoritative simulator cost.       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This exploits diversified starts already generated by the function while avoiding the     │
│                          │ cost of optimizing every constructed schedule. It is particularly effective for           │
│                          │ transactional conflict graphs because a greedy prefix can look good initially while       │
