│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ beam_conflict_ordering                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ Replace random sampled greedy construction with a deterministic beam-search ordering      │
│                          │ strategy followed by transaction relocation improvement.                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. The previous method evaluates only up to ten random remaining transactions at each     │
│                          │ position, so it can miss the transaction whose placement produces the smallest            │
│                          │ conflict-induced makespan.                                                                │
│                          │ 2. The new construction evaluates every feasible next transaction for each retained       │
│                          │ partial schedule using `workload.get_opt_seq_cost`. This directly optimizes the           │
│                          │ simulator’s actual makespan objective rather than proxy properties such as transaction    │
│                          │ size or write count.                                                                      │
│                          │ 3. A beam of up to `num_seqs` promising partial orders is retained. This avoids           │
│                          │ committing to one early greedy choice: different low-cost conflict-resolution orderings   │
│                          │ can survive until later operations reveal which one is best.                              │
│                          │ 4. Scores are cached by transaction-order tuple. Beam paths can request the same partial  │
│                          │ order, and local search repeatedly evaluates related schedules; caching prevents          │
│                          │ duplicate simulator calls.                                                                │
│                          │ 5. After construction, insertion-based local search moves every transaction to every      │
│                          │ possible position. This can repair decisions that were locally attractive while           │
│                          │ preserving the best complete beam result. A move is accepted only when it strictly lowers │
│                          │ actual makespan.                                                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The returned schedule remains a permutation of all transaction IDs, while the search now  │
│                          │ uses conflict-aware objective evaluations throughout instead of random candidate          │
│                          │ sampling.                                                                                 │
