│ patch_name               │ multistart_conflict_local_search                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the single sampled greedy construction with a multi-start objective-driven search │
│                          │ and an insertion-based local optimizer.                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Each greedy decision evaluates the simulator’s actual `get_opt_seq_cost` for every     │
│                          │ possible next transaction, rather than inspecting only a small random subset. This        │
│                          │ directly accounts for read/write conflict dependencies and their resulting critical path. │
│                          │ 2. Run several independently randomized starts, using `num_seqs` as the number of         │
│                          │ candidate schedules to construct. Randomized tie ordering provides diversification where  │
│                          │ several prefix choices have equal immediate cost.                                         │
│                          │ 3. Keep the best complete schedule across all starts.                                     │
│                          │ 4. Improve every constructed schedule with best-improving transaction insertion moves.    │
│                          │ Moving one transaction from one position to another can remove delayed conflict chains    │
│                          │ that greedy prefix construction cannot repair.                                            │
│                          │ 5. Cache schedule costs because the greedy and local-search phases can evaluate the same  │
│                          │ prefixes or complete schedules repeatedly.                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The result remains valid because every candidate is always a permutation of all           │
│                          │ transaction identifiers, while substantially expanding the search beyond the previous     │
│                          │ one-start, ten-sample greedy strategy.                                                    │
