│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ beam_vnd_scheduler                                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ This implementation replaces single-path greedy construction with a beam-search scheduler │
│                          │ followed by variable-neighborhood descent.                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Beam search keeps many promising partial transaction orders instead of committing to   │
│                          │ one greedy choice early.                                                                  │
│                          │ 2. Every candidate is scored using the authoritative simulator makespan function.         │
│                          │ 3. The beam retains alternative conflict-ordering patterns that a normal greedy strategy  │
│                          │ would discard.                                                                            │
│                          │ 4. Final beam schedules are diversified by positional distance, so local search starts    │
│                          │ from different scheduling basins.                                                         │
│                          │ 5. Variable-neighborhood descent evaluates relocation, swap, and segment-reversal moves,  │
│                          │ allowing coordinated corrections to transaction ordering.                                 │
│                          │ 6. For very small workloads, exhaustive permutation search is used to guarantee the       │
│                          │ optimal schedule.                                                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This improves makespan because it searches globally during construction and locally after │
│                          │ construction, rather than relying on one irreversible greedy ordering.                    │
