│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ beam_vnd_budgeted                                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ The current approach uses a beam width of `num_seqs` and only two relocation passes on    │
│                          │ the single best beam result. Its main limiting parameter is the fixed two-pass            │
│                          │ local-search cap: a relocation improvement can expose additional improvements, and swap   │
│                          │ moves can repair schedules that no single relocation can improve.                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This version retains simulator-scored beam construction, but changes the optimization     │
│                          │ configuration as follows:                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ - **Adaptive evaluation budget:** cache-miss budget scales with workload size and beam    │
│                          │ width instead of allowing only two local-search rounds.                                   │
│                          │ - **Multiple beam seeds:** terminal beam schedules are considered as distinct starting    │
│                          │ points instead of discarding all but one immediately.                                     │
│                          │ - **Variable-neighborhood descent:** repeatedly applies the best improving relocation     │
│                          │ move; when relocation stagnates, it evaluates swap moves. A successful swap restarts      │
│                          │ relocation descent.                                                                       │
│                          │ - **Strict-improvement termination:** search continues until true local stagnation or the │
│                          │ workload-size-aware evaluation budget is reached.                                         │
│                          │ - **Objective-based selection only:** every construction and local-search decision uses   │
│                          │ `get_opt_seq_cost`, directly optimizing conflict-induced makespan.                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This gives the optimizer more opportunities to correct early beam decisions while         │
│                          │ bounding runtime through the number of uncached simulator evaluations.                    │
