│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ block_neighborhood_search                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Replace first-improvement relocation with a steepest-descent variable-neighborhood search │
│                          │ evaluated by the simulator’s exact conflict-aware makespan.                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Step-by-step:                                                                             │
│                          │ 1. Evaluate every single-transaction relocation and retain the best strict improvement    │
│                          │ rather than accepting the first one encountered. This avoids committing to an early move  │
│                          │ that prevents a larger makespan reduction.                                                │
│                          │ 2. If relocation alone cannot improve the order, evaluate transaction swaps. Swaps can    │
│                          │ improve conflict overlap when two transactions must exchange positions but neither        │
│                          │ transaction has a beneficial independent relocation.                                      │
│                          │ 3. If both single-transaction neighborhoods stagnate, evaluate contiguous two-transaction │
│                          │ block relocations. In transactional workloads, strongly related transactions can need to  │
│                          │ move together: moving either one alone may temporarily worsen read/write conflict timing, │
│                          │ while moving their ordered pair can reduce the critical path substantially.               │
│                          │ 4. Every accepted move is a valid permutation and is scored through `get_opt_seq_cost`,   │
│                          │ so the search optimizes the actual simulator objective rather than a proxy heuristic.     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The block neighborhood is only explored after relocation and swap have failed, keeping    │
│                          │ the additional evaluation cost bounded while escaping common local minima.                │
