╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ block_relocation_descent                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ Add a contiguous two-transaction block relocation neighborhood to the existing exact-cost │
│                          │ local search.                                                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. The current relocation move can only move one transaction at a time. Some conflict     │
│                          │ reductions require two adjacent transactions to move together: moving either transaction  │
│                          │ individually can retain the same dependency delay, while moving their ordered pair        │
│                          │ before/after another transaction removes the delay.                                       │
│                          │ 2. The new move removes every adjacent pair and reinserts it at every other valid         │
│                          │ position. Every candidate is evaluated through the existing cached authoritative `cost()` │
│                          │ function, so decisions directly optimize simulator makespan rather than surrogate         │
│                          │ transaction statistics.                                                                   │
│                          │ 3. When ordinary relocation stagnates, compare the best swap and best block relocation.   │
│                          │ Select the strictly best improving move, then allow subsequent relocation passes to       │
│                          │ exploit the newly reached ordering basin.                                                 │
│                          │ 4. The move preserves schedule validity because it only removes and reinserts existing    │
│                          │ transaction IDs, maintaining a complete permutation.                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This is a bounded variable-neighborhood descent that broadens the search without          │
│                          │ replacing the effective greedy construction and single-relocation optimization already    │
│                          │ present.                                                                                  │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
