│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ beam_vnd_scheduler                                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ This implementation replaces single-path greedy construction with a conflict-cost beam    │
│                          │ search. Instead of committing to one transaction at each position, it keeps multiple      │
│                          │ promising partial schedules and expands each using `get_opt_seq_cost`, preserving         │
│                          │ alternatives that may lead to lower final makespan.                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Step-by-step:                                                                             │
│                          │ 1. Build a beam of partial transaction orders.                                            │
│                          │ 2. Expand each beam state with every remaining transaction (or a bounded candidate sample │
│                          │ for large workloads).                                                                     │
│                          │ 3. Score every append using the simulator’s authoritative makespan function.              │
│                          │ 4. Keep a diverse set of low-cost partial schedules, with randomized tie-breaking to      │
│                          │ avoid repeatedly following equivalent greedy paths.                                       │
│                          │ 5. Fully evaluate the best beam completions.                                              │
│                          │ 6. Apply best-improvement variable-neighborhood descent using relocation, swap, and       │
│                          │ reversal moves.                                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The beam search explores multiple global ordering basins before local optimization, which │
│                          │ avoids many of the irreversible decisions made by purely greedy construction.             │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
