│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ elite_beam_descent                                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ The beam search already produces several complete, conflict-aware candidate schedules,    │
│                          │ but the current code discards every final beam member except the single lexicographically │
│                          │ first minimum-cost result before local search. This can miss better local minima because  │
│                          │ schedules with equal or near-equal prefix cost can have substantially different           │
│                          │ downstream conflict critical paths.                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This edit adds a cached simulator-cost wrapper and performs the existing exact            │
│                          │ variable-neighborhood descent from several elite final beam schedules rather than only    │
│                          │ one. The simulator remains the sole scheduling objective: every relocation, swap, and     │
│                          │ block move is evaluated using actual makespan. Caching avoids repeated simulator calls    │
│                          │ when local-search neighborhoods overlap across elite candidates. The best locally         │
│                          │ optimized elite schedule is returned.                                                     │
│ num_applied              │ 3                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0430                                                                                   │
