│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ destroy_repair_restarts                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ Add deterministic destroy-and-repair restarts after the existing beam and local-search    │
│                          │ phase. The current descent is exact-cost based, but relocation and swap neighborhoods can │
│                          │ still become trapped in a local optimum. A restart removes three transactions from        │
│                          │ well-separated positions, retains the relative order of all other transactions, and       │
│                          │ greedily reinserts each removed transaction at the position with the lowest               │
│                          │ simulator-measured makespan. This creates a substantially different feasible permutation  │
│                          │ while preserving useful structure from the incumbent.                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Each repaired schedule is then passed through the established exact relocation/swap       │
│                          │ descent, so only simulator-validated improvements are retained. The search budget is      │
│                          │ enlarged and a restart reserve is kept while processing beam seeds, ensuring that         │
│                          │ restarts receive enough evaluations for both repair and subsequent local improvement      │
│                          │ rather than being starved by earlier seed searches.                                       │
