│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ beam_local_scheduler                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ This version combines exact cost-based greedy selection with a broader beam-search        │
│                          │ construction and stronger local improvement.                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. For very small workloads (`<= 8` transactions), it evaluates every transaction         │
│                          │ permutation and returns the true optimal makespan.                                        │
│                          │ 2. For larger workloads, it keeps multiple promising partial schedules rather than        │
│                          │ committing to one greedy prefix. Each beam expansion uses `workload.get_opt_seq_cost`, so │
│                          │ selection is based on the actual simulator conflict model.                                │
│                          │ 3. The beam retains diversified prefixes, preventing all candidates from collapsing into  │
│                          │ the same immediate greedy choice.                                                         │
│                          │ 4. The strongest completed beam schedules are improved with complete relocation and swap  │
│                          │ neighborhoods. Relocation is particularly important because it can move a transaction     │
│                          │ before the conflicting transaction responsible for its delay.                             │
│                          │ 5. Cached simulator calls avoid recalculating makespans for repeated prefixes and         │
│                          │ local-search candidates.                                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This improves on single-prefix greedy scheduling by preserving alternatives until later   │
│                          │ conflict information is available, then refining those alternatives with exact local      │
│                          │ makespan evaluations.                                                                     │
