│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ beam_greedy_vnd                                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ This version combines simulator-scored beam construction from the current implementation  │
│                          │ with the randomized greedy prefix selection from the crossover program.                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Step-by-step improvements:                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Exact search for very small workloads**: all permutations are evaluated when there   │
│                          │ are at most eight transactions.                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Simulator-scored beam search**: partial schedules are expanded and ranked using      │
│                          │ `get_opt_seq_cost`, so choices reflect actual read/write conflict delay rather than       │
│                          │ transaction length heuristics.                                                            │
│                          │ 3. **Greedy multistart crossover**: several randomized starting transactions construct    │
│                          │ schedules by choosing the next transaction with the smallest actual prefix makespan. This │
│                          │ preserves the useful greedy idea from the inspiration implementation while avoiding its   │
│                          │ single-start limitation.                                                                  │
│                          │ 4. **Diverse beam retention**: beam candidates are selected with preference for distinct  │
│                          │ final transactions, preventing all search paths from collapsing into one similar prefix.  │
│                          │ 5. **Variable-neighborhood local improvement**: complete schedules are optimized with     │
│                          │ relocation, swap, reversal, and coupled block relocation moves, all evaluated by the      │
│                          │ simulator.                                                                                │
│                          │ 6. **Perturb-and-descend**: the best local optima are lightly perturbed and optimized     │
│                          │ again to escape local minima.                                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ All candidate decisions use the workload simulator's exact schedule cost, directly        │
│                          │ targeting lower makespan from transaction conflicts.                                      │
