│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ restricted_pair_relocation                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ Add a restricted two-transaction relocation neighborhood after one-transaction relocation │
│                          │ and swap moves stagnate.                                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. The existing relocation move can only reposition one transaction. Some conflict chains │
│                          │ require two non-adjacent transactions to move together before the critical conflicting    │
│                          │ transactions, so neither transaction has an improving individual relocation.              │
│                          │ 2. The new move first identifies a small set of high-impact transaction positions. Impact │
│                          │ is measured with the authoritative simulator by removing each transaction and observing   │
│                          │ the resulting prefix/order makespan; transactions whose removal reduces cost most are     │
│                          │ likely contributors to the current critical path.                                         │
│                          │ 3. It considers every pair among these promising positions, removes both while retaining  │
│                          │ their current relative order, and reinserts the pair as a block at every possible         │
│                          │ destination.                                                                              │
│                          │ 4. This broadens the search beyond adjacent swaps and individual relocation without the   │
│                          │ prohibitive cost of testing every transaction pair. Every candidate is scored by          │
│                          │ `get_opt_seq_cost`, preserving exact makespan optimization and schedule validity.         │
│                          │ 5. The pair move is only invoked after the ordinary local neighborhoods fail, so it acts  │
│                          │ as an efficient basin-escape mechanism rather than adding unnecessary work to every       │
│                          │ descent pass.                                                                             │
