├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ deterministic_destroy_repair                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ Replace random two-relocation perturbations with a deterministic destroy-and-repair       │
│                          │ restart.                                                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Start from several already simulator-optimized local optima.                           │
│                          │ 2. Remove a small contiguous transaction segment while preserving the order of all        │
│                          │ remaining transactions.                                                                   │
│                          │ 3. Reinsert each removed transaction by evaluating every possible insertion position with │
│                          │ the exact simulator makespan.                                                             │
│                          │ 4. Try both the original and reversed removed-block orders, since coupled conflicting     │
│                          │ transactions can need to cross one another together.                                      │
│                          │ 5. Run the existing VND descent from the repaired result.                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This is stronger than random kicks because every repair decision is based on the actual   │
│                          │ conflict-derived makespan. Removing a short block can cross local-optimum barriers that   │
│                          │ cannot be improved through an individual relocation, while reinserting against the fixed  │
│                          │ residual order keeps the search focused and permutation-safe.                             │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
