│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ exact_pair_repair                                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the sequential greedy reinsertion used by destroy-and-repair with an exact joint  │
│                          │ repair for a removed pair.                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. The existing repair scores the first removed transaction against an incomplete         │
│                          │ schedule and irrevocably commits to its best partial insertion position.                  │
│                          │ 2. That partial choice can be wrong: the best position for one transaction often depends  │
│                          │ on where its coupled conflicting transaction is inserted.                                 │
│                          │ 3. The new method removes two adjacent transactions, preserves all other transaction      │
│                          │ order, and evaluates every pair of reinsertion positions under both pair orders using the │
│                          │ full simulator cost.                                                                      │
│                          │ 4. This exactly finds the best schedule in this destroy-and-repair neighborhood,          │
│                          │ including cases where the two transactions must cross different conflict boundaries       │
│                          │ together.                                                                                 │
│                          │ 5. Pair repair is deliberately used instead of a three-transaction greedy repair: it is   │
│                          │ exhaustive but remains computationally bounded at O(n²) simulator evaluations per         │
│                          │ restart, making it practical before the existing VND descent.                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The repair seeds and restart positions are retained, so this strengthens the current      │
│                          │ escape mechanism without replacing the effective beam search or local neighborhoods.      │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0460                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
